.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "virtual bool Assimp::ProgressHandler::Update (float percentage = \fR\-1\&.\fBf\fP\fP)\fR [pure virtual]\fP"

.PP
Progress callback\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpercentage\fP An estimate of the current loading progress, in percent\&. Or -1\&.f if such an estimate is not available\&.
.RE
.PP
There are restriction on what you may do from within your implementation of this method: no exceptions may be thrown and no non-const #Importer methods may be called\&. It is not generally possible to predict the number of callbacks fired during a single import\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Return false to abort loading at the next possible occasion (loaders and \fBAssimp\fP are generally allowed to perform all needed cleanup tasks prior to returning control to the caller)\&. If the loading is aborted, \fBImporter::ReadFile()\fP returns always nullptr\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "virtual \fBvoid\fP Assimp::ProgressHandler::UpdateFileRead (int currentStep, int numberOfSteps)\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
Progress callback for file loading steps\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fInumberOfSteps\fP The number of total post-processing steps 
.br
\fIcurrentStep\fP The index of the current post-processing step that will run, or equal to numberOfSteps if all of them has finished\&. This number is always strictly monotone increasing, although not necessarily linearly\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This is currently only used at the start and the end of the file parsing\&. 
.RE
.PP

